<title>POLAND: Poland sells PLN 300 mln floating 3-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Poland sells PLN 300 mln floating 3-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish treasury sold 300 million zlotys of floating three year bonds after investors bid for 364 million, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The minimum price of the bonds, which mature on August 6, 2000, was 97.82 and the average price was 98.07.</p>
<p>The value date for the tender is August 5, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
